V8's debug::ScopeIterator gained the pure virtual DeclaresLocals(), but the
DrumBrake (WebAssembly interpreter) scope iterator wasn't updated, so
v8_enable_drumbrake=true fails to build ("allocating an object of abstract class
type 'DebugWasmInterpreterScopeIterator'"). It only reports the module scope;
return true like the compiled-Wasm iterator (DebugWasmScopeIterator) does.

--- a/v8/src/debug/debug-wasm-objects.cc
+++ b/v8/src/debug/debug-wasm-objects.cc
@@ -853,6 +853,8 @@
 
   debug::Location GetEndLocation() override { return {}; }
 
+  bool DeclaresLocals() override { return true; }
+
   bool SetVariableValue(v8::Local<v8::String> name,
                         v8::Local<v8::Value> value) override {
     return false;
